    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Kristal",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115796291533018694650/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIuNi6nr7UYfcuoAmd8vLopfmmodGVtdbW1GLEiAP0EA-zaPQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "2 months ago",
        "text": "I had a very uncomfortable experience shopping at this store!  Be aware!\n\nI came in looking for Coconut oil. I was originally going to go to Rachelle Bery but decided to try this one instead.\nWhile in the Coconut oil section reading the descriptions and choosing the product I wanted, the jar I did not intend to buy accidentally slipped from hand and fell to the floor, shattering completely.\n\nThe glass jar broke and was only being held together by the hardened oil inside.\n\nThe manager came out from the back and immediately stated, “Store policy is if you break it, you buy it.” And that if I refused to pay, they would take my license plate number and involve the police, and that it would be a “long, unnecessary process” that she had “seen before.” She said she personally may not like the policy, but that it was the Owner’s rule and she had no choice but to enforce it.\n\nI explained that accidents happen, and before I could finish speaking, she cut me off and compared the situation to a car accident where you injure/really hurt someone, saying you have to assume your responsibilities. I told her she was comparing apples and oranges, then asked her doesn’t the store have insurances for accidents like this and was told again it was just “store policy.” The cashier then added that there is supposedly a sign on the front door.\n\nI asked what would happen if the accident had been a child, or if I could not afford both the broken item and the replacement. She told me the police would still be called regardless . I made it clear  that no one was going to run away, and that the way this was being handled was unfair. I also told her this policy would drive customers away, and she replied that they have already lost customers and that it “doesn’t matter” this is the “owner’s policy”.\n\nIn the end, after being threatened with legal action I paid under pressure.\nI was charged $12 for the Shattered Glass Jar of completely unusable Coconut oil and full price for a second unbroken one. The manager offered me $5 off and asked what I was using the oil for (I told her oral use), and to make matters worse — she says “ maybe just use on your hair and skin and not in the mouth” even though she had just forced me to purchase it.\n\nThe broken jar was full of dangerous tiny glass shards, yet I was still forced to buy it  and she even suggested I still use it on my body.\n\nAccidents while shopping happen. Threatening customers with the law over a simple accident and forcing them to buy unsafe, unsellable broken merchandise is NOT OKAY!\n\nI will never return to this store, and I strongly encourage everyone to beware.",
        "time": 1765545935,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Monique Orrell",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100131552790619908348/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVrT5I8ISNi_5XwpGJda29vcB4Kxwybnt1RfxSWQawyfLtFa3Tc=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "4 months ago",
        "text": "I discovered Biotope, when I was looking for a product that they carry which was also carried by a local store in my area (West Island) and they didn't have stock, so I drove over to Vaudreuil and they had lots of stocks and different variety, these are low carb pasta and the brand is called La Sublime, the pasta is frozen, and you really do not miss regular pasta. It tasted exactly the same. I can't comment on the rest of the store because the only thing I have bought there was those pastas but the staff is very nice and welcoming and very polite and helpful.",
        "time": 1759605346,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Masoud M",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104894776345607645484/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUoANk7hMGLU1a0Fkbimhx0ONMR1HyUtLcW2cQtyPemohuiHdyh=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 4,
        "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
        "text": "Prices are slightly high but quality has not been compromised! If you care about healthy food and quality ingredients and don't mind the costs, here is the place for you!",
        "time": 1766895508,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "carmela scrocca",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108894074529942171215/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWR1-7_yPS0UkHBwPJdnQYXVC3yRo3PAq7Z2zrEbK9T-CSo6miX=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
